WEBVTT

intro-1
00:00:04.350 --> 00:00:05.994
Providers work in their EHR.

intro-2
00:00:05.994 --> 00:00:09.577
Health-Connect's EHR write-back
is designed to deliver alerts

intro-3
00:00:09.577 --> 00:00:10.986
into the provider's EHR.

intro-4
00:00:10.986 --> 00:00:13.101
It is built, and it is sandbox only.

intro-5
00:00:13.101 --> 00:00:15.215
It isn't live with any customer yet.

optional-1
00:00:16.350 --> 00:00:18.504
Health-Connect itself stays optional:

optional-2
00:00:18.504 --> 00:00:23.103
a place to dig into the data behind an
alert, or to work a prior authorization.

settings-1
00:00:25.550 --> 00:00:28.769
Each connection has one
settings row, badged Sandbox.

settings-2
00:00:28.769 --> 00:00:33.688
This synthetic athena sandbox connection
is disabled, production isn't permitted,

settings-3
00:00:33.688 --> 00:00:35.753
and every saved change is audited.

routing-1
00:00:42.050 --> 00:00:44.515
Routing works by recommendation class.

routing-2
00:00:44.515 --> 00:00:48.083
Orders go to a provider,
care-team items go to a queue,

routing-3
00:00:48.083 --> 00:00:51.392
and documentation goes to
the CDI department queue.

close-reasons-1
00:00:54.900 --> 00:00:59.398
Close reason ids map Health-Connect
outcomes, dismissed, expired,

close-reasons-2
00:00:59.398 --> 00:01:02.651
or superseded, to the
EHR's own action reasons,

close-reasons-3
00:01:02.651 --> 00:01:05.904
so a sandbox case closes
with the right reason.

pause-1
00:01:13.450 --> 00:01:15.986
Any connection can be
paused with a reason,

pause-2
00:01:15.986 --> 00:01:18.344
and a global pause stops all write-back.

pause-3
00:01:18.344 --> 00:01:20.703
Pending deliveries are held, not failed.

attention-1
00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:34.282
The needs-attention list shows only the
bundles an admin has to look at, with ids,

attention-2
00:01:34.282 --> 00:01:36.637
states, and codes, never patient data.

attention-3
00:01:36.637 --> 00:01:39.798
This seeded sandbox bundle
carries fixture history:

attention-4
00:01:39.798 --> 00:01:42.524
its case was created in
the sandbox earlier,

attention-5
00:01:42.524 --> 00:01:45.685
and it's now held after too
many delivery attempts.

bundle-1
00:01:48.700 --> 00:01:52.181
The bundle page explains why
it's held, lists its items,

bundle-2
00:01:52.181 --> 00:01:53.922
and keeps an event timeline.

bundle-3
00:01:53.922 --> 00:01:56.719
Admin actions never send
anything themselves.

bundle-4
00:01:56.719 --> 00:01:58.708
The dispatcher does all sending.

release-1
00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:06.586
Releasing the hold is audited
and lands on the timeline.

release-2
00:02:06.586 --> 00:02:08.874
On this local stack no dispatcher runs,

release-3
00:02:08.874 --> 00:02:11.632
so nothing new is sent
and no vendor is called.

panel-1
00:02:16.900 --> 00:02:21.597
In the review workspace, the alert
carries a read-only EHR write-back panel,

panel-2
00:02:21.597 --> 00:02:25.738
badged Sandbox: the case number,
the route, and the delivery state.

panel-3
00:02:25.738 --> 00:02:28.519
That delivery is seeded
sandbox fixture data,

panel-4
00:02:28.519 --> 00:02:31.177
and nothing on this
stack reached a vendor.

closing-1
00:02:32.500 --> 00:02:34.940
EHR write-back is built and sandbox only,

closing-2
00:02:34.940 --> 00:02:38.214
designed to meet providers
in the EHR they already use,

closing-3
00:02:38.214 --> 00:02:42.261
with Health-Connect there for deeper
review and prior authorization.

disclosure-1
00:02:43.500 --> 00:02:47.310
A note on this recording: the
narration uses a synthetic voice,

disclosure-2
00:02:47.310 --> 00:02:51.786
and all data shown is synthetic demo
data, not a live customer deployment.
